 very relevant in the  upcoming episodes in this scene  reiner reveals that he wants to become  an honorary malayan so that his mother  and father can live together  but the underlying motivation beneath  that is that he also wants to become a  hero to the world  by eliminating the devils on the island  this is partly why later in the episode  he convinces the other warriors to  continue with the mission  even after marcel had died just before  we move on  the anime showed us this scene of a  young aaron inside the walls  and we previously saw this same moment  during season 1  in which armin showed aaron a book about  the outside world  this book is what sparked aaron's desire  to see the ocean  and free himself from the confines of  the walls and it just so happened that  on this same day  you know reiner was stating his desire  to become a hero  moving on the flashback then has a small  time skip  in which we get this suicide squad style  introduction to the new titan shifters  by this point reiner has inherited the  armored titan as as we knew he would  and he helps take down an enemy nation  alongside his fellow warriors  it was pretty awesome seeing all seven  of these titans in action at the same  time  not to mention seeing marcel's draw  titan as well for those who've missed my  previous review  marcel is the brother of porco who is  the current draws titan in the present  day  this whole sequence is basically meant  to show us why mali was so confident  in sending four children to invade  parodies island  having just crushed an enemy nation with  ease surely these kids would be able to  steal the founding titan from within the  walls  and wipe out the aldians who were living  there i mean it didn't work out but who  knows  maybe if the founding titan was someone  other than this maniac  then they you know maybe they might have  succeeded the scene then moves over to  porco threatening reiner as he just  can't believe that the bootlegger has  actually managed to nab himself  a titan shifter as porco is held back by  his brother  reiner notices that there's something  off about marcel but we'll explain that  later  these four candidates were the ones  selected for the invasion of the island  but the beast titan and the cart titan  were left at home  because you know if you send all the  titans at once then marley's going to be  very vulnerable and so that's why they  kept behind  zeke and peak during the parade reiner  spots his estranged father who is not an  aldian he is a malayan citizen  and throughout his childhood reiner was  kind of led to believe that if he became  a warrior and  by default if you're a warrior you are  also a citizen of mali  then he thought he'd be able to live  with his parents but as we can see you  know his father wanted nothing to do  with him  and basically considers reiner to be a  mistake the anime then progresses to the  invasion of the island  and as the kids make their journey  towards the walls they stop for a brief  moment and gather around the fire  it was here that we discovered why  marcel was acting strange  with the reason being that poco was  actually meant to be the armored titan  but marcel did everything in his power  to kind of like hurt his brother's  reputation  and at the same time put rhino on a  pedestal he did this to protect his  younger brother because you know there  are many  dangers associated with being a titan  with the curse of ymir being the most  obvious  marcel tearfully apologizes to rhino for  what he did  but just as reiner is processing this  information a random titan appears out  of the ground  and literally tries to eat him there and  then this titan was yamir  and prior to this moment she'd been a  pure titan for about 60 years  the reason she appeared was because the  sunlight provides energy to the pure  titans  and with the sun rising you know she had  the energy she needed  to get up and have some breakfast  luckily for rainer marcel pushed him out  of the way  saving his life in the process after  fleeing the scene  reiner is confronted by annie who wants  to abandon the mission  and return to mali annie's plan was to  return home  after finding whoever stole the draws  titan which is ymir like i said  in her words she didn't think the  mission could succeed without marcel's  leadership  rainer insisted that they persevere with  the plan to invade the walls  and he had a few different reasons  number one was that he wanted to save  his own skin and avoid being  you know avoid being eaten by the next  armored titan and reason number two  is that he kind of you know he wanted to  be a hero so that people would respect  him  and that's the part that he didn't say  out loud being a hero was his secret  motivation for continuing the plan  and after annie had beaten the crap out  of him reiner promised that he would  fill the void  that marcel left behind once they  arrived at the wall  bertolt smashed through the gate as we  know but he was then confronted by a  titan which could very easily have eaten  him  this titan used to be dinah fritz who is  the mother of zeke jaeger  and the former wife of grisha any other  titan would have eaten bertos in this  situation  but as we know this pure titan is  special not only does she have royal  blood flowing through her veins  but before she was transformed she  promised grisha that she would find him  somehow  it cannot be a coincidence that she said  these words and then immediately when  the opportunity arose  she went to grisha's house and ate his  new wife this titan only had one goal in  mind  and it was to find grisha and because  she's a titan of royal blood  i am certain that the parts that connect  all aldeans played a role  in her discovering grisha's family home  not to mention finding eren again later  in the series  if she was anyone else then bertolt  would have lost the colossal titan at  this moment  guaranteed anyway reiner and the gang  were able to sneak into the walls thanks  to all the chaos  and in this scene we can see that armin  mikusa and aaron  are among the refugees later on the  warriors meet a man from a small village  in the mountains  who tells them his story of how his  family was eaten by titans  after that man killed himself the three  of them decided to adopt his story as  their own  very disrespectful of them but you gotta  do what you gotta do  five years after they arrived on the  island annie was the main member of the  group who was actually  you know following through with the  mission based on the info they had  the king was in possession of the  founding titan and so annie began to  follow a mysterious man in a black coat  who was one of the royal government  officials this man was kenny ackerman  aka levi's favorite uncle and he started  working with the royals after his  dangerous encounter  with the previous king of the walls  after catching her by surprise  she made up some random story about how  she was looking for her long lost father  before attempting to kick him can we  just appreciate how powerful her kick  was in this moment  because i mean she knocked a brick out  of position and she's not even in her  titan form so  that's pretty impressive while annie  escaped kenny was able to get a glance  at her face  which put the entire plan in jeopardy  kenny could easily blow her cover  especially if she got close to the royal  family so for that reason  annie wanted to abandon the mission yet  again but reiner actually had a good  plan this time around  instead of abandoning the mission reina  proposed that they get the founding  titan to reveal  himself and suggested that they attack  wall rose  this plan proved to be successful  because once the colossal titans smashed  the gate and let all those titans in  the ensuing violence is what led to  aaron awakening his titan powers  the flashback ends with this moment of  eren in the cadets  and this is when he was struggling to  master the odm gear he asks reiner how  he can improve  because obviously you know if you can't  master the oem gear  then how could he get revenge on the  titans like he promised he would in this  brief moment  reiner is reminded of himself as a young  child reiner helps aaron up  and tells him that the only thing he can  do to get better and accomplish his  goals  is just to keep moving forward that line  is super important at the end of this  episode  so make sure you remember it this  flashback scene was then interspersed  with images  of rhino loading up his gun in the  present day as he prepares to pull the  trigger  and just end everything at this point in  time reiner is just tired of living  and everything he's been through has  just taken its toll on him  and he he feels like he has nothing left  to live for just as he goes to pull the  trigger  falco coincidentally bangs on the wall  in frustration  which interrupts rhino falco's  frustration stems from the fact that  he's not good enough to surpass gabby  and he realizes that something needs to  change if he's ever going to inherit the  armored titan  if not for this moment from falco rhino  would have died there and then  and the power of the armored titan would  have been passed to a newborn alien  child  somewhere in the world the bang on the  wall gave falco a second to reconsider  what he was doing  and he realized that he does still have  something to live for which is the  remaining warrior candidates  the episode ends with falco walking past  the hospital as the soldier that he  helped in the previous episode  waves towards him as they continue to  speak falco tells the soldier about his  fear that he won't be able to inherit  the armored titan  as there's another talented candidate  that everyone loves  as falco begins to feel sorry for  himself his words are virtually  identical to what aaron was saying  earlier in the episode  when he was failing to master the  maneuvering equipment the soldier is  clearly touched by what falco was saying  and begins to wonder about why a person  goes to war  as he says some people are forced to do  it by outside factors  such as the aldians that we saw on the  front line during episode 1.  on the other hand you have people who  willingly charge into this hell  like rhino when he insisted they  continue with the mission on two  separate occasions  the soldier says that people who force  themselves to go into war  are different from those who are forced  by external factors  as it's likely that the people who force  themselves see something that others  don't  whatever that motivating factor is the  man says that you'll never be able to  find it out  unless you keep moving forward and that  was the conclusion of this episode  just in case i didn't make it clear  enough in that last line the man is  quoting what rhino previously said  to him major spoiler warning ahead if  you haven't realized it by now  but the soldier that falco is talking to  is in fact aaron yeager  we'll get into the details of how and  why it's possible another time  but the last line of episode 2 made it  very obvious  that this man is who we think he is let  me know in the comments if you realize  who this was before watching this video  or seeing this title  but anyway guys that was the breakdown  for episode three  i'd appreciate if you dropped a like if  you liked it and please do share it with  anyone who you think  might enjoy watching it until the next  one peace out

